 Mobile native filter sheets keep their own bar anchor. When lower viewport space is sufficient, the sheet remains 8px below the bar; otherwise placement flips above or clamps inside viewport safety margins with positive scrollable height, including offscreen layout changes. Placement is recalculated on owned-root/window scroll and resize; original modal/focus cleanup remains required. For this overlayCompatibility V1 implementation, the below-bar offset applies only when lower viewport space is sufficient; upward/clamped placement is its explicit boundary exception. Migrated mobile nodes are weak keys in the renderer logical-parent/anchor registry: the registry does not strongly retain its keys, remove deletes associations, and scope disposal releases modal registrations and viewport listeners. Foreign-root insertion remains rejected.
+
+## Independent document preferences
+
+`contract.json.preferences` is the data contract for same-origin independent documents. Read and write the declared localStorage keys. Theme missing defaults to `syncWithSystem`; resolve that value using the declared media query. Keep `dark-2` as the theme while using dark color scheme. Locale missing or empty defaults to `en`; use the published supported list and aliases, with `en` fallback for unsupported values. Native getLang returns stored text; SDK consumers normalize it through the aliases/list. Do not infer language from navigator or import host SPA modules.
+
+Read again on load/refresh and on cross-document `storage` events. The writing document must update its own view: browsers do not dispatch a storage event to that writer. Changes to system preference must re-resolve the system theme. This descriptor stores no user data elsewhere and grants no business permission. Consume it only from a successful CI and exact promoted image digest.
